{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026690-spooky-spooky-skeletons-death-magic-questions","id":1026690,"title":"Spooky spooky skeletons/ Death magic questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-04T14:25:27-08:00","id":1026690,"title":"Spooky spooky skeletons/ Death magic questions","content":"Hey guys! Ill probably be playing a death mage not sure between the concepts of a pretty creepy and cannibal thyrsus learning death arcanum or a savage moros learning life and spirit. So i wanted to ask u guys some clarifications on death related spells<br /> <br /> _1/ can death 3 rip away and severe the soul of.both humans and supernaturals? Can i steal the soul of a blood.talon or a. Daeva?<br /> <br /> 2/ if i touch someone and send him across the Twilight and then cose the gate, (ghost gate spell) unless he has some way to escape or travel between worlds, he is effectively trapped and hopeless right?<br /> <br /> 3/ can someone cast some light on why souls are so powerful and meaningful to steal? They are unique yantra for magic and if i eat them i can become immortal being a tremere for example?<br /> <br /> 4/ will we ever be able to see an actual rule written legacy for the tremere lich or do i have to do the math and convert and adapt it from the first edition <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 5/ unless there is the resonant condition on a location or a target, a ghost cannot manifest or influence a being or a place right?<br /> <br /> For example if a ghost of a.dead girl is obsessed with fear and knives unless there is fear in the air or knives she wont be able.to use her powers across the twilight?<br /> <br /> 6/does the anchor of a ghost need to be physical or can it also.be a concept or an idea?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance and have a nice supernal day","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T14:34:03-08:00","id":1026694,"title":"","content":"1) Mortals only, minor templates probably with a Reach. I'd say a vampire's soul is on the same level as an Awakened one, on the other hand I think there's some debate about if vampires even have souls.<br /> <br /> 2) Basically.<br /> <br /> 3) Steal a soul, get a living zombie servant (Effectively if you keep track of your victims anyway), the unique yantra, reaper legacies benefit from them, and also they're good for trade.<br /> <br /> 4) If Dave follows up on his latest remarks about the Tremere they will no longer be a legacy but a corruption of your Gnosis. Which I assume can look similar and be completely different.<br /> <br /> 5) Right, but the Resonant Condition is usually pretty easy. For instance, hack up a lung's worth of ectoplasm on a thing and you're good to go.<br /> <br /> 6) Has to be physical either an person, place or object.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-04-2017, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T15:03:36-08:00","id":1026713,"title":"","content":"Ghost Gate is weird. Generally there has to be an active effect to keep something material in a state of Twilight. If it isn't naturally in Twilight it should pop right back once the spell ends, but that's not how the spell is written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T15:38:04-08:00","id":1026720,"title":"","content":"It's not really all that different from how going into the Shadow, or the Underworld or the Astral works, once you translate from one metaphysical state of existence to another then you may remain there until you translate back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T15:43:53-08:00","id":1026724,"title":"","content":"My question is this. If you open a gate to the Twilight and then leave it open can stuff from Twilight come wandering out, like a ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T15:50:34-08:00","id":1026735,"title":"","content":"As long as its open to the right frequency of Twilight (In this case Death) it should be possible. Although if the ghost isn't under the Open condition then it will likely snap immediately back into Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T15:52:19-08:00","id":1026737,"title":"","content":"Even though you didn't pay for the scale to allow others through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T15:53:36-08:00","id":1026738,"title":"","content":"No. The wording doesn't even actually allow material entities to come back either, but I'm guessing that's not intentional. Either way a manifestation would be required for ghosts to become material. That's not what Ghost Gate does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T16:03:06-08:00","id":1026746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026690-spooky-spooky-skeletons-death-magic-questions?p=1026737#post1026737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even though you didn't pay for the scale to allow others through.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scale for Ghost Gate would only make sense as effecting the size of the gate itself. Although the number of targets it effects would matter if you were using the variant with +1 Reach that can transfer you without the actual gate-y bit.<br /> <br /> Anyway <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> is correct about why a ghost going through the Ghost Gate wouldn't matter, no granted Manifestation so not able to maintain a Manifested form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T16:11:03-08:00","id":1026749,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Devourers_of_Flesh\" target=\"_blank\">Devourers of the Flesh</a> are a nice legacy for Thyrsus cannibals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T18:28:01-08:00","id":1026799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> _1/ can death 3 rip away and severe the soul of.both humans and supernaturals? Can i steal the soul of a blood.talon or a. Daeva? </div> </div> </div>Given how the reason you need Death 5 to severe a mage's soul is that their Gnosis &quot;clings&quot; to the soul, I say a similar justification holds true for a lot of supernaturals and thus would require Death 5. Those without such factors would be viable for Death 3, maybe 4. For example, vampires have the Beast interfering, but ghouls probably don't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2/ if i touch someone and send him across the Twilight and then cose the gate, (ghost gate spell) unless he has some way to escape or travel between worlds, he is effectively trapped and hopeless right? </div> </div> </div>I'd rule that the normal effect of the spell, tuning whatever passes the 2-d film into ghost-Twilight, is Lasting. However, the +1 Reach effect of the spell, tuning the subject into ghost-Twilight directly, is non-Lasting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3/ can someone cast some light on why souls are so powerful and meaningful to steal? They are unique yantra for magic and if i eat them i can become immortal being a tremere for example? </div> </div> </div>Well, souls are mystifically significant in just about every human culture, even though each one has different definitions of what a soul is. The in-universe theory is that souls are made up of all the five Subtle Arcana, hence the part where they can be used as a Yantra for spells of those five Arcana. It's also the most intimate &quot;organ&quot; of yours, and intimacy itself has magical weight.<br /> <br /> And eating/claiming/consuming souls don't automatically make you a Tremere. Mages who do that are called Reapers. The Tremere are a special hybrid of Reapers and Liches (mages who abandon humanity in the process of trying to overcome mortality). They are a Legacy whose membership is big enough to qualify as a Nameless Order, and I think it was hinted before that unlike other Reaper/Lich Legacies, they might actually be a different template altogether, what with having absorbed many other Reaper Legacies into them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4/ will we ever be able to see an actual rule written legacy for the tremere lich or do i have to do the math and convert and adapt it from the first edition <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Until supplements come out, we can't be sure. If you do a conversion, please share them in the forums <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5/ unless there is the resonant condition on a location or a target, a ghost cannot manifest or influence a being or a place right?<br /> <br /> For example if a ghost of a.dead girl is obsessed with fear and knives unless there is fear in the air or knives she wont be able.to use her powers across the twilight? </div> </div> </div>Technically, it's the Anchor Condition for ghosts. The Resonant Condition is for spirits and Goetia.<br /> <br /> Ghosts can work on someone or something with the Anchor Condition keyed to them, using their Influences or other means of interaction, to strengthen it into the Open Condition, after which the majority of their Manifestations start working. There are Manifestations that do not require Open, or require more than that. When ghosts Manifest, they leave a bunch of ectoplasm on the vicinity, which counts as the Open Condition for any ghost.<br /> <br /> A ghost's Influences and Anchors don't always match exactly, although they will be related. The ghost of a jealous lover maybe Anchored to her living lover, using her Influence over Jealousy to wreck havoc on any romantic relationships the lover gets into, so that the lover may remains hers and hers only forever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6/does the anchor of a ghost need to be physical or can it also.be a concept or an idea? </div> </div> </div>I think the Anchor itself has to be physical. We do have examples of ghosts anchoring themselves to a concept of death - those are called Geists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T19:16:17-08:00","id":1026812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lasombra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026690-spooky-spooky-skeletons-death-magic-questions#post1026690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">_1/ can death 3 rip away and severe the soul of.both humans and supernaturals? Can i steal the soul of a blood.talon or a. Daeva?</div> </div> </div> </div> You're going to have to ask your ST to answer that one. Going by the rules of the Astral, only human beings (mortals, hunters, mages, probably deviants) have actual souls; even the Begotten don't have souls. So, its up to the ST if Awakened magic can touch whatever passes for a pseudo-soul in non-humans. Keep in mind that there's also zero rules for what happens with a non-human loses their soul-replacement, leaving many to speculate that its not possible for these supernaturals to lose their souls while alive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2/ if i touch someone and send him across the Twilight and then cose the gate, (ghost gate spell) unless he has some way to escape or travel between worlds, he is effectively trapped and hopeless right? </div> </div> </div> The way I'm reading the spell, it seems that, once the duration ends, everyone in Twilight state returns to material. Considering that you can use +1 Reach to bypass the &quot;gate&quot; requirement, it would make no sense for Duration to do nothing in this case.<br /> <br /> Remeber, Twilight isn't a realm, its a state of being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3/ can someone cast some light on why souls are so powerful and meaningful to steal? They are unique yantra for magic and if i eat them i can become immortal being a tremere for example? </div> </div> </div> Honestly? Souls are overrated. Souls are necessary in order to Awaken, and losing one is kind of detrimental to one's health. They're really only relevant for individual Obsessions or perhaps a Mystery or two to study, if so desired. Souls mainly come up in either Reaper stories, or some kind of monster story that uses them for something (Abyss?), otherwise they're not a big deal. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4/ will we ever be able to see an actual rule written legacy for the tremere lich or do i have to do the math and convert and adapt it from the first edition <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div> Comments were made early on that its going to be doubtful to see the Reaper Legacies, including the Tremere, redone with Left Handed Legacies being published so recently. Not sure how much is true, or how reliable my memory is, so take it all with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> Everyone else touched on the last two fairly well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T23:43:12-08:00","id":1026887,"title":"","content":"Just read a comment from Dave last night that Mages can rip the soul out of a Beast with Death 5, I assume this means other major splats are also viable targets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T00:34:27-08:00","id":1026900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026690-spooky-spooky-skeletons-death-magic-questions?p=1026887#post1026887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just read a comment from Dave last night that Mages can rip the soul out of a Beast with Death 5, I assume this means other major splats are also viable targets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering he's also posited the theory that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950625#post950625\">the &quot;soul&quot; mages can remove might be a character's Temenos</a> and Beasts are the only non-mage splat that <i>have</i> a Temenos, I wouldn't put money on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T00:51:36-08:00","id":1026905,"title":"","content":"Hmm, fair enough. That could explain why Mage souls are different than other types of souls found in the CofD lines. Do you think he actually meant Oneiros though? Because I thought the Temenos was a kind of collective thing, although I could see it if it's ripping out the human's connection to the Temenos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T01:05:32-08:00","id":1026909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026690-spooky-spooky-skeletons-death-magic-questions?p=1026905#post1026905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, fair enough. That could explain why Mage souls are different than other types of souls found in the CofD lines. Do you think he actually meant Oneiros though?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=989287#post989287\">I'm fairly confident he didn't.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because I thought the Temenos was a kind of collective thing, although I could see it if it's ripping out the human's connection to the Temenos. </div> </div> </div>The nature of sympathy means the difference between &quot;this is a single mental dimension that every human soul connects to&quot; and &quot;this is a mental dimension that every human soul contains a copy of that reproduces alterations made inside every other copy of it&quot; is sort of academic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T01:12:46-08:00","id":1026913,"title":"","content":"Huh, I had not thought of that. Trippy. It raises questions of what you can do as a result of that, like can you isolate one person's Temenos without removing it in order to create a nearly (Only nearly since obviously the person would still be capable of changing his Temenos bit by bit as he thought of the various things in it) static record of the Temenos at one point in time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-05-2017, 04:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T01:32:42-08:00","id":1026920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026690-spooky-spooky-skeletons-death-magic-questions?p=1026913#post1026913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, I had not thought of that. Trippy. It raises questions of what you can do as a result of that, like can you isolate one person's Temenos without removing it in order to create a nearly (Only nearly since obviously the person would still be capable of changing his Temenos bit by bit as he thought of the various things in it) static record of the Temenos at one point in time?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's possible to freeze a person's Temenos, it's almost certainly at least the stuff of multi-degree Mastery, but the trickier part is that the Temenos is not normally altered by singular people's private thoughts and its natives include a lot of archetypes that are basically different takes on the same concept and imagery in places that you navigate to by following the thematic markers that correspond to your intended destination, so observing that the isolation is holding would require a fairly exhaustive range of confirmation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T01:50:28-08:00","id":1026928,"title":"","content":"*Adamantine Arrow reads post: Red Lists character*<br /> <br /> *Guardians of the Veil reads post: Red Lists character*<br /> <br /> *Mysterium reads post: Black Lists character*<br /> <br /> *Silver Ladder reads post: Red Lists character*<br /> <br /> *Free Council reads post: Red Lists character*<br /> <br /> *Seers of the Throne reads post: Black Lists character*<br /> <br /> *House Tremere reads post: Red List &amp; Black List character, might lead to a new House if they develop any good skills on their own.*<br /> <br /> *The Scelesti reads post: Oh what the heck, we'll be your Hufflepuff.*<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry, I know this contributes nothing but those very well might be the exact 7 questions that an ST never wants to hear their players asking in regards to Mage the Awakening, and I LOVE IT! XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T04:10:23-08:00","id":1026959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026690-spooky-spooky-skeletons-death-magic-questions?p=1026909#post1026909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=989287#post989287\">I'm fairly confident he didn't.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>He clarifies his meaning more thoroughly here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=994774#post994774\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...774#post994774</a><br /> <br /> He also makes it clarifies some about which supernatural splats possess souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T04:19:35-08:00","id":1026960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026690-spooky-spooky-skeletons-death-magic-questions?p=1026920#post1026920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's possible to freeze a person's Temenos, it's almost certainly at least the stuff of multi-degree Mastery, but the trickier part is that the Temenos is not normally altered by singular people's private thoughts and its natives include a lot of archetypes that are basically different takes on the same concept and imagery in places that you navigate to by following the thematic markers that correspond to your intended destination, so observing that the isolation is holding would require a fairly exhaustive range of confirmation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing you're of the opinion then that simply removing the Temenos from the person is not enough to disengage that instance of a Temenos from the Sympathetic link it has to all the others, right? Although from there it seems like it could be just a Mind or Space Shielding spell away...<br /> <br /> Although, difficulty of the feat aside I'm actually more interested in the idea that it could theoretically be done and what the consequences of doing so would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T11:14:44-08:00","id":1027161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026690-spooky-spooky-skeletons-death-magic-questions?p=1026960#post1026960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing you're of the opinion then that simply removing the Temenos from the person is not enough to disengage that instance of a Temenos from the Sympathetic link it has to all the others, right? Although from there it seems like it could be just a Mind or Space Shielding spell away...</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering we're talking about a world vastly larger than the limits of Area-based Scale sporting what is effectively at least a Connected sympathy with all other instances, yeah, it's a markedly less simple process than just walling off the middle layer of somebody's oversoul.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although, difficulty of the feat aside I'm actually more interested in the idea that it could theoretically be done and what the consequences of doing so would be. </div> </div> </div>I'm of the opinion that it's the stuff of archmastery to accomplish to a conclusive degree, so yeah, that's a pretty definite story catalyst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T12:54:11-08:00","id":1027230,"title":"","content":"thanks everybody for tha answers! i think i'll let other players manipulate or rip away souls of other splats only at death 5 or above, if it will ever happen (but i don't think it will be the case). Maybe adding some oder arcana for some supernaturals (like spirit for werewolves).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T06:17:34-08:00","id":1027579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026690-spooky-spooky-skeletons-death-magic-questions?p=1027161#post1027161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering we're talking about a world vastly larger than the limits of Area-based Scale sporting what is effectively at least a Connected sympathy with all other instances, yeah, it's a markedly less simple process than just walling off the middle layer of somebody's oversoul.<br /> <br /> I'm of the opinion that it's the stuff of archmastery to accomplish to a conclusive degree, so yeah, that's a pretty definite story catalyst.</div> </div> </div> </div>Continuing speculation, if the soul is the Temenos and its Sympathetically connected to all other Temenos such that a change in one can change all the others wouldn't that mean you could theoretically use a soul to Sympathetically affect or remove the soul of any other Mage, human or Beast?<br /> <br /> Also, you have a Temenos in material form, could you use it like a viewing port into the Astral with the appropriate magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T08:50:49-08:00","id":1027700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1026690-spooky-spooky-skeletons-death-magic-questions?p=1027579#post1027579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Continuing speculation, if the soul is the Temenos and its Sympathetically connected to all other Temenos such that a change in one can change all the others wouldn't that mean you could theoretically use a soul to Sympathetically affect or remove the soul of any other Mage, human or Beast?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts have a hard lockout on sympathetic soul-removal baked into the way the template works, assuming the &quot;spell has to be cast within the Lair&quot; limitation takes the existence of sympathetic casting into account, the souls of most non-Beast Temenos-possessing entities do not regularly descend into it, and the rules of sympathetic magic mean that being able to actually target a specific person obviates pretty much any benefit you'd derive from using a different soul in a casting besides destroying it for the universal sacrament bonus.<br /> <br /> Might be a neat basis for a Reaper Legacy, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, you have a Temenos in material form, could you use it like a viewing port into the Astral with the appropriate magic? </div> </div> </div>Hard to say, given the cost of entry on one hand and phenomena like Los Angeles' big Mystery on the other.<br /> <br /> Engaging with Synesi through The Outward and Inward Eye is close to an idea as I've got at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T09:24:21-08:00","id":1027711,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that the Tremere have actually removed their natural Sympathetic connection to the Temenos and thus humanity by drowning their soul in the Ocean Ouroboros. Instead it has to be artificially maintained via their victim's souls. Like they even needed a way to be more monstrous...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}